Anti-Ban Lua overlay
====================

These seven scripts come from "Anti Beta (PC + Mobile)" by Lão Ký
(https://github.com/LaoKy/MiniWorld-Anti-Ban-Cheat-Beta), used under the MIT
License. They are stock Mini World 1.7.15 scripts with a firewall patch:
member->host attack messages (crash invite, teleport pull, remote HP kill,
fake vote-kick, GameVm skybox/weather) and WS chatpush kicks (gm.kick,
device_limit_kick, fake room invite) are dropped, and a device-id rotation
is applied for anti-ban. gm.lua additionally drops the in-game GM console
(loadstring/setfenv/io.open), which is a hardening, not a loss of anything
this mod menu uses.

The original mod ships as a 32-bit-only APK, but nothing here is
architecture specific: it is Lua bytecode inside assets/script_res.pkg, and
the stock .so of the anti build is bit-identical to ours (md5 6f1c805c...).
scripts/repack.sh overlays these files onto the stock pkg via tools/pkgwrite.py,
so the 64-bit bundle gets the same anti-ban.

accountmanager.lua carries local modifications on top of Lão Ký's work:
the firewalled device_limit_kick popup left a server ban (device/IP/UID)
with no UI at all, so the client hung on the modal loader instead of going
back to login. msr_ban_logout(code) now spots the ban error codes on every
login-fail path, toasts the message and returns to the login frame. Two
diagnostics sit next to it: msr| breadcrumbs through gFunc_LogTimeStamp
(plain print never reaches logcat, so they show up in a fox-log capture
instead), and a watchdog on the auth ShowNoTransparentLoadLoop/Hide pairs
- a login the server never answers at all releases the loader and returns
to login after 20 seconds rather than hanging for good. The account-login
button specifically lands in loginV2ByAuthInfo, which blocks in
data_update() with no loader window of its own (so the window watchdog
never arms there); it therefore carries its own watchdog arm that also
closes the conn, unwinding the stuck stack through its own error branch.
For diagnosis the file also wraps the global Show/HideNoTransparentLoadLoop
pair with observe-only breadcrumbs (show/hide/hook on) - the login frame
calls those globals directly, so before the hook a stuck modal loader was
invisible in a capture log - and logs the data_update result as
msr|l2v2 code=..., since this path has no ban-check call to report it.
A main-thread heartbeat (msr|beat every 5s via MiniUIScheduler) closes the
set: the lobby-phase freeze shows no loader at all, so a gap between beats
is the only way to pin the second the lua main loop wedged from a log.
The file
keeps its full source embedded in the Lua debug field; to rebuild it, extract
that source, patch it, compile with chunkname = source and run
tools/luatranscode.py to convert the luac dump to the engine's chunk format
(4-byte size_t + rotated opcode block).

